From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:56:51 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Retain authenticated candidate bodies in a bounded volatile
 pool

Integration note (2026-10-15): the original source commit had no message body.
This explanation is supplied by the series integrator; source diff bytes are unchanged.

Retain exact header/BlockID/framing/transaction-root authenticated bytes under explicit
resident, decode and pin limits. Immutable pins survive pool destruction, pinned
bodies cannot be evicted, and availability epochs never wrap. Retention does not
claim contextual block validity. Allocation-failure, corruption, limits and lifetime
tests pass; exact validation scope is recorded in the implementation plan.

